  data: {
    LLM: "If your team has two out of the three top cards (Red Joker, Trump Ace, Black Joker), bid at least 7. The probability of losing a trick is low when you control the 'Master Trio'.\n\nTeam Coordination: Since you have two partners, watch who wins the early tricks. If partner A1 wins with a King, don't waste your Queen to 'over-win'; save it for the next round to exhaust the opponent's cards.\n\nThe Joker Lead: Lead the Black Joker if you want to flush out the Red Joker early. This clears the way for your Trump Ace to become the most powerful remaining card.",
    Player: "If your team has two out of the three top cards (Red Joker, Trump Ace, Black Joker), bid at least 7. The probability of losing a trick is low when you control the 'Master Trio'.\n\nTeam Coordination: Since you have two partners, watch who wins the early tricks. If partner A1 wins with a King, don't waste your Queen to 'over-win'; save it for the next round to exhaust the opponent's cards.\n\nThe Joker Lead: Lead the Black Joker if you want to flush out the Red Joker early. This clears the way for your Trump Ace to become the most powerful remaining card.",
